"""Per-repository template for tools/build_notebook.py (NOTEBOOK_SPEC 2.2 §4 standalone carrier).

Only the task-specific prose and stage cells live here. Runtime install, the embedded pipeline
modules (pipeline.py, metrics.py, samples.py), and the model pin/stage/verify cells are produced by
the generator from repository sources so they cannot drift from the package.

This template configures an E2E visual-question-answering workflow: the pinned Salesforce/blip-vqa-base
snapshot is digest-verified and loaded, the annotations of a digest-pinned VizWiz-VQA shard are read
column-only and 240 pinned photographs taken by blind users are fetched one by one, validated and split
by image, seven authored questions over a drawn scene are answered through the inference contract, the
frozen model is scored on the held-out photographs beside two non-neural baselines, a bounded
fine-tuning of the answer decoder's last blocks runs, the held-out split is scored again per category
and per answerability, the adapted model re-answers the drawn scene, and the adapter is exported and
reloaded.

Review fixes (Notebook Review Framework v1, review PR #7, VQA-M1..M6 / VQA-m1..m5): the runtime is the fleet's uv
isolated environment (no in-kernel install, no restart); the notebook no longer calls majority match ungameable or
`other` answerable, and prints how often each system answers `unanswerable` and how its content answers score, so
the reading it teaches is the one the run measures; no held-out result is asserted, and the notebook says that the
default hyperparameters were compared on a test split, so the test gain is optimistic; every re-run of Sections
5-7 starts from the pretrained model; the BYOD contract states the enforced minimum, replaces an earlier upload,
keeps zip sub-folders under a guarded root with size limits, names a missing records file and records BYOD
provenance; a question about written text runs from a provided cell; and the guided layer (how to use, roadmap,
predictions, worked answers, a change-one-thing activity, troubleshooting, glossary, conclusion) is added.
"""
