        "the adaptation contract works end to end on a real out-of-distribution VQA corpus, the model learns the corpus's "
        "answerability convention from 140 examples, and that answer log shows that this sample gives **no "
        "evidence of better answers to answerable questions**. Whether a different recipe could add that is an open question "
        "this notebook does not settle.\n\n"
        "The size of the gain is also **optimistic**: the default configuration was compared with others on a test split in "
        "the build record, so the test split is not independent evidence for the default settings. Within a run, validation "
        "alone chooses the epoch. The test split is 60 photographs from one seeded draw of one shard of one corpus, the "
        "validation split that picks the epoch is 40, the metrics are four reference-based scores (own implementations of the "
        "VQA accuracy convention and DocVQA's normalisation, none a human judgement), and VizWiz's ten answers disagree often "
        "enough that `unanswerable` sits among the accepted answers of many questions. So a gain here says the contract "
        "works, not that the adapted model is better on your photographs, that it reads text, counts, or localises, or that "
        "its answers are faithful — it now says `unanswerable` to photographs it could have answered, and it can still answer "
        "wrongly. Fine-tuning on a narrow corpus can also erode the model elsewhere; the drawn scene re-answered in Section 9 "
        "is one image of evidence about that, not a measurement.\n\n"
        "Four things to carry to real data. **Baselines first:** the constant-answer and question-prefix baselines and the "
        "frozen model's score on *your* accepted answers are the numbers to read before any adapted one, on every metric — "
        "no metric is immune to a constant answer when one answer dominates. **Decompose the gain:** when an answer such as "
        "`unanswerable` or `no` is common, report how often the model gives it and how its other answers score, as Section 8 "
        "does. **Selection:** choose settings on validation only, and keep a test split you look at once. **Leakage and "
        "targets:** keep every question on an image in one split (the contract does this), split by photographer or session "
        "when your images come from few sources, and remember that the training target is the majority answer — a corpus "
        "whose annotators often say `unanswerable` trains the model to say it.\n\n"
        "Successful execution proves that the recorded repository revision's pipeline modules, carried in this standalone "
        "notebook, can acquire and digest-verify the pinned model snapshot, fetch and digest-verify the annotations and "
        "photographs of a real VQA corpus, validate the demonstrated dataset contract without leakage, execute the inference "
        "contract and a bounded fine-tuning, evaluate against two trivial baselines and the frozen model on an image-disjoint "
        "split, and emit the shown machine-readable artifacts — without the repository being reachable. It does **not** "
        "establish benchmark superiority, VQA accuracy on any other population or camera, a lift on answerable questions, a "
        "usable answerability threshold, or production fitness.\n\n"
        "**Optional experiments (they do not affect the default path).** Each one changes one form field; note the numbers "
        "you want to compare first (the Section 8 run history keeps one row per pass). In Colab, **Runtime → Run after** runs "
        "the selected cell and every cell below it; Sections 5, 6 and 7 reload the pretrained model before they use it, so no "
        "experiment inherits an earlier adaptation.\n\n"
        "- **A learning rate too small to move the model:** Section 10.\n"
        "- **One epoch:** set `EPOCHS = 1` in Section 7, select Section 7 and choose **Run after**; compare the share of "
        "`unanswerable` answers and the `answerable` column with the default run (the first epoch is where the convention "
        "is learned).\n"
        "- **More trainable blocks:** set `TRAINABLE_DECODER_LAYERS = 4` in Section 7, select Section 7 and choose **Run "
        "after**; compare the artifact size, the share of `unanswerable` answers and the content VQA accuracy.\n"
        "- **More epochs:** set `EPOCHS = 6` in Section 7, select Section 7 and choose **Run after**; watch whether validation "
        "VQA accuracy keeps rising or turns (the best epoch is kept either way).\n"
        "- **Another split:** change `SPLIT_SEED` in Section 4, select Section 4 and choose **Run after**; read how much the "
        "frozen and adapted scores and the share of majority-`unanswerable` test questions move with a different draw.\n"
        "- **Another sign:** edit `SIGN_TEXT` or `SIGN_QUESTION` in Section 11 and run that cell alone.\n"
        "- **Your own photographs:** BYOD (Section 4, then **Run after**); read the two baselines, the frozen score and the "
        "answerability breakdown before the adapted number.\n\n"
        "## Troubleshooting\n\n"
        "- **Section 1 stops with \"needs a Linux x86_64 runtime\".** The locked environment is built from manylinux wheels. "
        "Use Google Colab, Kaggle or a Linux Jupyter server; Windows and macOS kernels are not supported.\n"
        "- **Section 1 fails while downloading** (`uv` wheel, Python build or packages). The runtime needs PyPI and the "
        "python-build-standalone download; run the cell again once the network is back. A \"size/SHA-256\" or \"does not "
        "match its digest\" error means a file was altered: do not edit the cell, regenerate the notebook from the "
        "repository.\n"
        "- **\"The isolated environment's Python process exited\".** Usually the runtime ran out of memory. Restart the "
        "session and choose **Run all**; on CPU, close other notebooks first.\n"
        "- **Out of disk, or the checkpoint download stops.** The locked install, the 1.54 GB checkpoint and the 113 MB of "
        "photographs need a few GB of free space. Start a fresh runtime, or delete `dimer_isolated_env/` and `weights/` from "
        "an earlier attempt.\n"
        "- **A digest or size mismatch in Section 3 or 4.** A download was incomplete or altered; the notebook refuses it "
        "rather than continuing. Run the cell again; never edit the manifest or the image pins.\n"
        "- **The VizWiz image host is slow or refuses requests in Section 4.** The cell retries transient errors with a "
        "pause; if it still fails, wait and run Section 4 with **Run after** again. Photographs already fetched are reused "
        "from `weights/vizwiz/` after their digest is checked.\n"
        "- **BYOD is refused in Section 4.** The message names what to fix: a split left with too few records (at least 12 "
        "records on 12 different images), no or several records files, an image path that does not exist relative to the "
        "records file, an empty answer list, a duplicate id, a zip over the member or size limit, or a member outside the "
        "upload folder. Fix the zip and run Section 4 with **Run after** again. An empty or cancelled upload asks you to "
        "choose a file or set `BYOD_PATH`.\n"
        "- **Section 8 says \"not improved\" or \"the selector kept epoch 0\".** Not an error: under these settings no "
        "adaptation beat the frozen model on validation, or the kept epoch did not beat it on test. Read the epoch history in "
        "Section 7; the export and reload in Section 9 still run.\n"
        "- **Reload parity fails in Section 9.** The saved adapter does not reproduce the evaluated model. Re-run from "
        "Section 7 (it reloads the pretrained model first), or restart the session and choose **Run all**.\n"
        "- **Numbers differ slightly from the recorded runs.** CPU and GPU arithmetic differ, and because decoding is "
        "autoregressive one different token changes an answer; a few hundredths of VQA accuracy between a T4 and a CPU run "
        "are possible on 60 questions. Larger differences on the default settings mean a form field was changed.\n"
        "- **You re-ran the routing cell in Section 1.** It starts a new isolated process and discards every variable "
        "created so far; choose **Run all** again.\n\n"
        "## Glossary\n\n"
        "- **Accepted answers / majority answer:** the ten human answers VizWiz collected per question, and the most "
        "frequent of them, which is the training target.\n"
        "- **`unanswerable`:** VizWiz's answer for a photograph that cannot answer the question (blur, framing, darkness, "
        "the object out of view).\n"
        "- **Category:** the answer type VizWiz assigns (`other`, `unanswerable`, `yes/no`, `number`); it is not the same "
        "as the majority answer.\n"
        "- **Greedy decoding:** generating each next token as the single most likely one; reproducible, but not a quality "
        "guarantee.\n"
        "- **Token budget (`max_new_tokens`):** the most tokens the model may generate; `truncated` says the budget ran out.\n"
        "- **VQA accuracy:** for each question, `min(number of human answers equal to the prediction / 3, 1)`, averaged; "
        "partial credit when one or two annotators agree.\n"
        "- **Exact match / majority match:** the prediction equals any accepted answer / the majority answer.\n"
        "- **ANLS:** Average Normalised Levenshtein Similarity — a string-similarity score that gives credit for near-misses.\n"
        "- **Baseline:** a system with no model (here a constant answer and a question-prefix lookup) that shows what any "
        "useful model must beat.\n"
        "- **Answerability breakdown:** for each group of questions, how often a system answers `unanswerable`, how much of "
        "its VQA accuracy those answers earn, and how its other (content) answers score.\n"
        "- **Fine-tuning / trainable blocks:** further training on labelled examples; only the named decoder blocks may "
        "change, the rest stay frozen.\n"
        "- **Epoch / validation selection:** one pass over the training records; the epoch kept is the one with the highest "
        "validation VQA accuracy (epoch 0 = the frozen model).\n"
        "- **Training / validation / test split:** photographs used to train, to choose the epoch, and to report the final "
        "result once; split by image so no photograph is in two splits.\n"
        "- **Optimistic estimate:** a test score of a configuration that was chosen by looking at test scores.\n"
        "- **Adapter / reload parity:** the saved trained tensors, and the check that a pipeline rebuilt from them gives the "
        "same answers.\n\n"
